* Passing Arrays as Arguments
- In function two ways pass a variable - pass by value -pass by refrence
-array comes in pass by refrence category because it chnages in main method and pass by value does not changeable.
-code:-
import java.util.*;
import java.lang.*;
import java.io.*;

// The main method must be in a class named "Main"
class Main {
    public static void update(int arr[]){
for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
arr[i]=arr[i]+1;
}
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int arr[]={90,95,99};
update(arr);
System.out.println("Marks");
for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
System.out.println(arr[i]);
}
}
}

// output:-
Marks
91
96
100


-length method used to find the size of the array
-in function defination write [] bracke this denoted the array refrence .

